A||||5||ocalafiero1||2.5 liter Timing/ ocasional stalling||||1||
Z||000000||ocalafiero1||09-04-2001||10:24 PM||||My '86 is running again. I went into diagnostic mode and set the timing(sort of) the timing mark seems to fluctuate a degree or two either way with the light on it. I went ahead and got it as close as possible on #1 & #4, and tightened the distributor back down. While road testing, everything was great, until I got almost home and the chime (not sure if it was seatbelt or what) pinged once and the car stalled. I rolled into the driveway and it started right up, and is still idling just a tiny bit rough with an ocasional "puff" through the exhaust. It seems to be a bit rich, but I'm not positive. I didnt get a check engine light or any codes from the stall.  The items that are new/replaced are: ECM, Distributor, Ignition Module, O2 sensor, Fuel pressure regulator, Coil, plug wires, plugs, fuel filter and fuel pump. Any help would be appreceated.<P>Thanks,<P>Mike<p>[This message has been edited by ocalafiero1 (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||OcalaFiero||09-05-2001||08:25 AM||||Bump! Anyone........Anyone......||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||09-06-2001||10:05 AM||||OcalaFiero,  Here are just a few threads on a similar topic (see below).  Is the 'puff' you described the same as the poot sound I referred to?  The stalling sounds like that might be unrelated to the stumble.  The stalling actually sounded like a bad ignition switch ie. it turned-off for a split second and the eng stalled and chime went off once.  Anyway I hope some of this helps you and hope to see you at the gathering.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011378.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011378.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/search.cgi" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/search.cgi</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012847.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012847.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 09-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||OcalaFiero||09-06-2001||10:19 AM||||that's one thing I didn't check, the Ignition Switch. I have a new column With tilt, etc) that I need to put in, I'll take a look at the switch when I do the swap. I guess I'll double check wiring continuity and maybe even look at the timing gears also. Thanks again and see you in October.<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||ocalafiero1||09-08-2001||10:37 PM||||She is now running great. The ignition switch was pretty corroded and had a lot of rus inside of it. The car starts up quickly and no more phantom shut offs. I'm going to replace the ignition lock also as there is a little play in it, but all is now well. Thanks to all, especially 87GTZ34.<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||ocalafiero1||09-10-2001||08:28 PM||||Well, I still had a slight miss, but I got it fixed. When the car was running rich and the converter clogged up, causing a nasty back fire, I cracked one of my plugs (slightly). I replaced the plugs today with good old AC/Delcos and now she purrs. Thanks all.<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
